Description:
I'm new to modding and while I was learning to make my own mod, I thought some people can benefit from this simple change.
<br />
<br />This mod may counteract against some game design, but I thought [b]fine ingredients should produce fine goods. [/b]
<br />
<br />[b]It basically overwrites all machines loaded at certain point in content pipeline[/b], so I assume this mod has some extreme compatiblity with other mods.
<br />
<br />[b]Side effects:[/b]
<br />1. Casks are practically obsolete.
<br />2. Large Milk potential value = Regular Milk potential value (Large Milk produces gold quality cheese by default)
<br />3. Items that cannot normally have quality (ex. Pickles and Jellies) get a quality.
<br />
<br />I may provide an update with configurable patch to address 2&amp;3.
<br />
<br />
<br />
<br />This mod does not use Content Patcher and edits all machine data from "Data/Machines" with the priority of: 
<br />AssetEditPriority.Late + 2
<br />
<br />Simple source code:
<br />[spoiler]
<br />[code]﻿private void OnAssetRequested(object? sender, AssetRequestedEventArgs e)
<br />{
<br />    if (e.NameWithoutLocale.IsEquivalentTo("Data/Machines"))
<br />    {
<br />        e.Edit(asset =&gt;
<br />        {
<br />            var data = asset.AsDictionary&lt;string, MachineData&gt;().Data;
<br />
<br />            foreach ((string machineId, MachineData machineData) in data)
<br />            {
<br />                if (machineData.OutputRules != null)
<br />                {
<br />                    foreach (var outputRules in machineData.OutputRules)
<br />                    {
<br />                        foreach (var outputItem in outputRules.OutputItem)
<br />                        {
<br />                            outputItem.CopyQuality = true;
<br />                        }
<br />                    }
<br />                }
<br />            }
<br />        }, AssetEditPriority.Late + 2);
<br />    }
<br />}[/code][/spoiler]
<br />
<br />That's it. Unless other mods are loaded/patched very late (priority 1003 and above), this will overwrite all machines if they have OutputRules.
<br />I've checked with Butter Churn from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/24842]Cornucopia - Artisan Machines[/url]﻿, and Chest/Hoppers with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/stardewvalley/mods/1063]Automate[/url].
<br />They are compatible.
<br />
<br />Thank you.
